@startuml fig3_12_unfair_means
' Figure 3.12 - Sequence Diagram (Part 8): Recording an unfair-means case with evidence photos.
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor #999999
skinparam SequenceGroupBorderColor #666666
skinparam SequenceDividerBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7
skinparam NoteBorderColor #B8A04A
hide stereotype
skinparam participant {
  BackgroundColor<<ui>> #FDEDEC
  BorderColor<<ui>> #C0392B
  BackgroundColor<<api>> #EAF7EA
  BorderColor<<api>> #2E8B57
  BackgroundColor<<alg>> #FEF5E7
  BorderColor<<alg>> #D68910
}

actor Admin
participant "React UI" as UI <<ui>>
participant "Express API" as API <<api>>
database MySQL as DB

== 9 · Unfair Means Case (examination department only) ==

Admin -> UI : Unfair Means → "Record a case"\n→ select exam session
UI -> API : GET /unfair-means/session-students?slot_id=X
API -> DB : SELECT students seated in slot X\n(individual_seating_plans JOIN seating_allocations\nJOIN classrooms JOIN students)
API -> DB : SELECT courses in slot X without a seating plan\n(course_enrollments; room / seat unknown)
API -> DB : SELECT invigilators on duty in slot X
API --> UI : { students[], on_duty[] }
Admin -> UI : Pick student, reporting invigilator, witness;\nfill category, time, description,\nmaterial seized, action taken
UI -> API : POST /unfair-means\n{ slot_id, roll_number, reported_by_user_id, ... }
API -> DB : BEGIN
API -> DB : Look up the student's course, room and\nseat in slot X (404 if not writing)
API -> DB : SELECT case WHERE slot_id, roll_number\n(409 if one already exists)
API -> DB : INSERT INTO unfair_means_cases\n(snapshot of student, course, room, seat;\nstatus = 'reported', recorded_by = admin)
API -> DB : COMMIT
API --> UI : { case: UFM-<year>-<id> }

Admin -> UI : Attach evidence photos (≤ 5)
UI -> UI : compressImage(): longest side\n≤ 1600 px, JPEG
UI -> API : POST /unfair-means/:id/photos\n(multipart: photos[], widths[], heights[], captions[])
API -> API : multer limits: ≤ 5 files, ≤ 5 MB each;\nsniffImage(): JPEG / PNG signature only
API -> DB : BEGIN; SELECT case FOR UPDATE\n(409 if the case is closed)
API -> DB : COUNT existing photos\n(400 if the total would exceed 5)
API -> DB : INSERT INTO unfair_means_photos\n(data MEDIUMBLOB)
API -> DB : COMMIT
API --> UI : { photos[] }

== Review and decision ==

Admin -> UI : Set status / record decision
UI -> API : PUT /unfair-means/:id/review\n{ status, decision_note }
API -> API : Final status (action_taken / dismissed)\nneeds a decision note
API -> DB : UPDATE unfair_means_cases SET status,\ndecision_note, decided_by, decided_at
API --> UI : updated case
note right of UI
  Closed case: details and photos
  are locked until it is reopened
  (status back to under_review).
  Cases are never deleted.
end note

== Case report PDF ==

Admin -> UI : Open case → "Download report"
UI -> API : GET /unfair-means/:id
API -> DB : SELECT case + photo list
API --> UI : case
loop each photo
  UI -> API : GET /unfair-means/:id/photos/:photoId
  API -> DB : SELECT mime_type, data
  API --> UI : image bytes
end
UI -> UI : jsPDF: case report, signature blocks,\nphoto annexure (2 per page)
UI --> Admin : UFM-<year>-<id> report (PDF)
@enduml
